:: How to Play {"position":"200,100","size":"100,100"}
(link-rerun: "Puzzles : ")[This game is very puzzle driven, to progress with the game you must have time and patience.
However not all puzzles are necessary, so remember that exploring is rewarding!]
(link-rerun: "Combat : ")[The combat in this game aims to have both scripted encounters and random encounters.
There also is a weapon system that is most likely going to be subject to change.
(link:"Learn more?")[{
	}(link-rerun: "Scripted Encounters?")[(dialog: [Scripted encounters will be things such as boss encounters, secret encounters, and other encounters that will be in every playthrough.], "Okay.")]
	(link-rerun: "Random Encounters?")[(dialog: [Some areas of the game will take place outside such as on the streets, in these areas there will be a random chance that in between Passages the player will have an encounter.], "Okay.")]
	(link-rerun: "Gun System?")[(dialog: [Make sure you first have a gun selected.
    Guns require you not only to have the gun and the proper ammuniton.
    Howevere while being in an encounter if you use a gun it can break rendering it useless.], "Okay.")]
	(link-rerun: "Knife System?")[(dialog: [Much like guns, knifes can break and if they do they will be rendered useless.], "Okay")] ] ]
(link-rerun: "Passages and Chapters : ")[Each different scene is a passage and each passge has text, any purple/blue text is interactable with.
Each chapter has a different ending based on the players choices. The player can make a multiple amount of choices in each chapter and each playthrough will be different.
(link-replace: "PSST...")[We do plan on having unique backgrounds for each passage but thats more of a end development goal.] ]
(link-rerun: "Saving and Loading : ")[Saving is done is the html local history, please ensure that your browser supports this.]
(link-rerun: "Audio : ")[Not all web browsers have audio support, this game has audio and it is recommended to play with audio.]
(link-rerun: "Browser Trouble Shooter : ")[(go-to: "TSL")]
[[Start->FakeStartScreen]]


